ontent (e.g. a distinct phrase introduced by the edit) rather than a generic word like 'agent', so the grep cannot pass on incidental matches.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5d","T5e","T7","T9"],"criteria":["E6","F1"],"decision":"advisory","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC1 check: `rg -n \"evidence location|agent\" docs/adr/0043-operator-attested-completion-evidence.md`","AC2 check: `rg -n \"ticket comment|non-material\" src/rebar/_guides/writing-a-passing-plan.md`","The word 'agent' is a generic term likely to occur incidentally; the pattern does not anchor to the specific distinction the criterion requires."],"finding":"AC1 and AC2 proving commands are loose substring greps that can pass without the criterion's semantic content actually being present. `rg -n \"evidence location|agent\"` matches any incidental occurrence of the word 'agent' (common in this codebase) without proving the ADR 'distinguishes evidence location from actor identity and permits agents to record concrete operator-attested evidence'. Likewise `rg -n \"ticket comment|non-material\"` can match without the guide actually instructing the author to record evidence in a ticket comment.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f2f15ec30cbbc97f2","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria, lines 1-2","norm_id":"n6f2633355a938ac7","priority":0.4813,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["The ADR is edited but retains the old actor-identity framing while still containing the word 'agent' elsewhere — AC1's grep passes anyway.","The guide already contains 'ticket comment' in an unrelated section — AC2 passes without the new instruction being added."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Anchor to a phrase the edit uniquely introduces, e.g. AC1: `rg -n \"evidence location.*actor identity|actor identity.*evidence location\"` (or a quoted sentence added to the ADR) and AC2: `rg -n \"record .* in a ticket comment\"`, pairing each with a manual review of the focused diff.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["2 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add an acceptance criterion that updates (or verifies) the completion-verifier remediation guidance so it directs recording [operator-attested] evidence in a ticket COMMENT (non-material), not the description, and demonstrate the deadlock no longer triggers.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T6","necessity","project.portability"],"criteria":["E3"],"decision":"dropped","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Report step 2: 'tag the criterion with the exact string [operator-attested]... the tag lives in the DESCRIPTION' — this guidance is what forces the staling description edit.","Acceptance Criteria only grep docs/adr/0043-...md and src/rebar/_guides/writing-a-passing-plan.md; no criterion updates the completion-verifier remediation text or the attestation-staling mechanism.","No criterion demonstrates end-state that the deadlock (tag-in-description -> stale attestation -> unrunnable re-review) no longer occurs."],"finding":"The plan's title promises resolving the close-gate deadlock, but its acceptance criteria only edit ADR 0043 and writing-a-passing-plan.md; neither touches the COMPLETION VERIFIER's remediation guidance that (per the report's step 2) instructs authors to add the [operator-attested] tag to the DESCRIPTION — the very edit that stales the plan-review attestation and drives the cycle. Without changing that instruction (or the mechanism that treats the tag as description material), the documented 'evidence lives in a non-material comment' contract may not actually prevent the deadlock it targets.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f0c6c72a67beb787f","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Title 'Close gates deadlock...' vs. Plan / Acceptance Criteria (ADR 0043 and writing-a-passing-plan.md only)","norm_id":"na1779a836ecabdd5","priority":0.2656,"reason":"veto:cited-reference-inaccurate","scenarios":["An author on a future pure-deletion ticket follows the still-unchanged verifier remediation, edits the description to add [operator-attested], stales the attestation, and re-hits the exact cycle the plan claims to close."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Include the completion-verifier remediation string among the edited surfaces, or add a criterion showing the deadlock scenario is resolved end-to-end (e.g., a walkthrough/test that adding attestation evidence does not stale the plan-review attestation).","tier":"LLM","validity":0.3125,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"no","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"insufficient","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"low","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Address cycle step 3 directly: either (a) make adding/removing the [operator-attested] tag a non-material checkbox annotation in the material fingerprint (mirroring the existing box-flip normalization at test_checkbox_flip_keeps_signed_material_valid), or (b) explicitly re-scope the ticket to the documentation clarification and update the title/cycle text so it no longer claims to resolve the deadlock.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan cycle step 3: 'Adding the tag EDITS THE DESCRIPTION, which stales the plan-review attestation.'","ADR 0043:39-40: 'An author marks a criterion operator-attested with an inline tag at the start of the checkbox text.'","docs/plan-review-gate.md:500: 'Adding evidence prose next to a ticked box IS an edit to description, and that does invalidate.'","The evidence-is-a-commen